    "# EXECUTION: scoring harness for limit-order entry/exit.\n",
    "# The swing signal decides *whether* to trade; this decides *at what price*. The bar to\n",
    "# clear is not the oracle -- it is a randomly chosen minute.\n",
    "harness = rs.ExecutionHarness(df_reg, df_min, deadline=380)\n",
    "\n",
    "for side in (\"buy\", \"sell\"):\n",
    "    mean, sd = harness.random_null(side)\n",
    "    print(f\"null ({side}, random minute vs TWAP): {mean:+.2f} bps, per-day sd {sd:.1f} bps\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df_exec = harness.sweep()\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.set_option(\"display.width\", 200)\n",
    "for side in (\"buy\", \"sell\"):\n",
    "    sub = df_exec[df_exec[\"side\"] == side].drop(columns=\"side\")\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n=== {side.upper()} -- {len(harness.days)} sessions, unconditional \"\n",
    "          f\"(forced fills in) ===\")\n",
    "    print(sub.to_string(index=False, float_format=lambda v: f\"{v:9.2f}\"))\n",
    "    best = sub.loc[sub[\"vs_twap_bps\"].idxmax()]\n",
    "    print(f\"best vs TWAP: k0={best['k0']}, gamma={best['gamma']} -> \"\n",
    "          f\"{best['vs_twap_bps']:+.2f} bps at {best['fill_rate']*100:.0f}% fill \"\n",
    "          f\"(if-filled-only would have claimed {best['IF_FILLED_ONLY_bps']:+.2f} bps)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\"\"\n",
    "--- how to read this ---\n",
    "k0=0 is 'market at the open', the do-nothing baseline. Anything that cannot beat both\n",
    "that and the random-minute null is not worth having.\n",
    "\n",
    "Watch the gap between vs_twap_bps and IF_FILLED_ONLY_bps: that gap IS the selection\n",
    "bias. It widens with k0, because more aggressive limits miss on exactly the days that\n",
    "ran away.\n",
    "\n",
    "NOT YET MEASURED, and it can invert the whole ranking: passive limits are structurally\n",
    "anti-momentum -- they fill when price comes to you and miss when it runs. If the entry\n",
    "signal is momentum, the unfilled days are the winners and this policy destroys alpha\n",
    "even while its execution stats look fine. Test by correlating (not filled) against the\n",
    "subsequent multi-day return, once a signal exists.\n",
    "\n",
